    "text": "<p>A disc of radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math> and mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>M</mi></math> is rolling horizontally without slipping with speed <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi></math>. It then moves up an inclined smooth surface as shown in figure. The maximum height that the disc can go up the incline is:</p><img src=\"assets\\qt0057_e611f14d5cbc.png\" style=\"width: 350px; height: 122px;\"/>"
  },
